# Thinkway Git Workflow (Branch Gate)

## Before any implementation

1. Run `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` (or equivalent).
2. **Allowed to proceed:**
   - `develop`
   - An approved `feature/*`, `hotfix/*`, or similarly named working branch **created from `develop`** (or from `main` only for an approved Production hotfix)
3. **If on `main` or any other disallowed branch:** stop. Switch to `develop` (or create/checkout the correct feature branch from `develop`) **before** editing files, committing, or pushing.
4. Do not implement, commit, or push feature work on `main`.

## Branch roles

| Branch | Role |
|---|---|
| `develop` | Authoritative development baseline — all new work starts here |
| `main` | Release / Production tip only — not a development branch |
| `feature/*` | Branched from `develop` → merge back to `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | From `main` for emergencies → merge to `main`, then **immediately** merge back to `develop` |

## Release path

```
develop → feature/* → develop → QA → main → approved Production deploy
```

Invariant: `main` must never permanently stay ahead of `develop`. See `docs/RELEASE_WORKFLOW.md`.
